title: NTLM Relay Activity
id: 1fdef163-98ab-4358-9744-bf1e2591b4e1
status: experimental
description: Detects likely NTLM relay, where an authentication received on one host is immediately used to authenticate to a different host with the same credentials within seconds, a hallmark of relay attacks.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1557/001/
logsource:
  category: network_connection
detection:
  selection:
    auth_protocol: 'NTLM'
    relayed: true
  condition: selection
fields:
  - src_ip
  - dst_ip
  - dst_port
falsepositives:
  - Rare legitimate credential delegation
level: high
tags:
  - attack.credential_access
  - attack.t1557.001
